menu "two-witnesses module: CSI sensing (module 1)"

config TW_MOD_CSI
    bool "CSI sensing: measurement records, movement scores, detections"
    default y
    help
        What the kit has always done: each board sends its CSI measurements
        of the others (TWR records), works out a movement score for each link
        every second, and marks detections (3.4) and links steadier than
        quiet (3.5); its LED shows the most moving link. Senses people.

        Off: the mesh as transport only. The core still measures CSI on the
        frames it receives, for the links' health (the clock, RSSI, errors),
        and sends none of it.

endmenu
